{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793390315,"nonce":"/w3WJHAHRyIiAyjcD32ffML88Ao=","message":"Items 6, 4, 5, 1, 3 and 9 of RayDE's list are in, local and unpushed. Pixel probes pass on hlwgpu and caribou-gpu.\n\n**What each commit adds**\n0f6b1ba55857b13d1302ed49d5681a7211d48040: DrawContext.pushBlendMode (normal, add, subtract, multiply, screen) and pushColorTransform (multipliers and offsets, nested ones concatenate). The path shader writes premultiplied colour now.\n10b8471ca24c116bb67831626fa6b251bca63166: DrawContext.pushMask(ctx -\u003e draw the mask) and popMask; draws between are kept by the mask's alpha. The mask is drawn into a texture of the target's size.\nd75831e6560d52c004f776f568592546e9a47528: Stroke.scaleMode (normal, none, horizontal, vertical), Stroke.onePixel() for hairlines, DrawContext.drawPath (fill then stroke). Curves, fill rules, caps, joins, miter limit and dashes already existed in Path and Stroke.\n54901794bf4ad0eb1ce5abdec7e9391572b9bdda: DrawContext.drawTriangles (vertices, indices, uvs, bitmap, culling) and drawQuads (source rects and a 2x3 transform per quad, optional alphas and colour transforms).\n6ae4cbc1000b5f010a28e3320e7017f0210dde0e: PixelSurface.bitmap() as a brush or image source, and DrawContext.image9 for scale9Grid.\n\n**Limits**\nBlend modes are the GPU's fixed blends. Overlay, hardlight, difference, invert, darken, lighten, layer, alpha and erase are not there: they read the target, and erase would also clear the page behind the canvas because a canvas draws into the shared frame.\nMultiply over transparent pixels leaves them transparent; Flash shows the draw as normal.\nMasks do not nest: an inner pushMask is ignored. A mask's own blend modes and colour transforms are ignored.\nTriangle and quad edges are not antialiased. A texture is mapped affinely per triangle, so uvt's perspective term is not read.\nPixelSurface.bitmap() encodes and decodes the whole surface after each write. A surface written every frame should use ctx.surface; sampling a live surface texture from a brush is not built.\ncacheAsBitmap needs nothing here. scrollRect is pushClipRect.\n\n**Still open here**\nItem 8 (text runs and metrics back to the app), which RayDE said is later. Filters and shaders (item 7) are out of scope.","files":null}]}